  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Initial Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the initial scope of the high-energy sports retail e-commerce application, CoreBuy/Velocity Sport. I\'m examining the images, design tokens, HTML, and requirements, beginning with the screenshots to establish a baseline understanding. My goal is to grasp the project\'s overall parameters.\n\n\n**Analyzing Home Screen Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the detailed elements of the home/explore screen. I\'m taking a close look at the notification bar, header, hero section, category carousel, trending products grid, and trust indicators. I\'m considering each section\'s purpose and functionality. I\'m also breaking down the mobile navigation. I\'m making notes.\n\n\n**Detailing Product Screens**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the Product Detail Screen (PDP). I\'m carefully dissecting the breadcrumb navigation, product titles, and pricing structures, which are all displayed in detail. I\'m focusing on the image gallery and its various view options, along with the size selector. The action buttons\342\200\224add to cart, buy now, and WhatsApp order\342\200\224are also areas of focus. I\'m also examining the trust badges. I have started breaking down the accordions.\n\n\n**Examining Checkout Flow**\n\nI\'m now deep in the checkout screens, breaking down each element. I\'m noting the progress indicators and the form fields, especially the custom styling of the sport-specific inputs. The order summary card is getting a close look, from line items to subtotals, tax, and the total. Finally, I\'m analyzing the payment options\342\200\224UPI, cards, and COD\342\200\224and the associated trust badges.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 8918257
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
